      "content": "How Learning About Behavioural Biases Improves Financial Literacy\nFrancisco Pitthan, K. De Witte\n\nNote: Knowledge about logical fallacies can support discipline in live trading and adherence to set, logical plans. \n\nThis paper is the closest peer reviewed example I could find which has research, not opinion. Although it's a behavioural finance paper it's not directly related to real-time decision making in markets which is why it's not included in #deleted-channel  \n\nThis study still shows clear mitigation in short-sighted biases in financial decision making which is quite close.",
      "author": {
