    {
      "id": "1423301198227701780",
      "type": "Default",
      "timestamp": "2025-10-02T14:30:49.315+01:00",
      "timestampEdited": null,
      "callEndedTimestamp": null,
      "isPinned": false,
      "content": "**The Profitability of Technical Analysis: A Review by Cheol-Ho Park, Scott H. Irwin**\n\nNote: This paper exposes the inconsistency and lack in edge if any for traditional technical analysis patterns. We choose to refute it through a more rigorous lens because people can argue that everyone analyses price differently and so on.\n\nWe believed a collection of papers and references about data snooping etc. would be more helpful. This paper also mentions it but I think that individual aspects, definitions and data analysis concepts should be understood on the surface before diving into more complex matters.",
