    {
      "id": "1423440361476325517",
      "type": "Default",
      "timestamp": "2025-10-02T23:43:48.419+01:00",
      "timestampEdited": null,
      "callEndedTimestamp": null,
      "isPinned": false,
      "content": "WARNING! Slightly more advanced than normal.\n\nThe existence of this paper (and others like it) made me smile a few years back. \n\nAs some of you know, me and Ron do have our proprietary things we use. One is the withdrawal optimisation. I figured out (with similar methods to this paper) the best time to withdraw money for a strategy to maximise returns and minimise edge decay negative effects. The optimal point to withdraw allows for you to make far more money over many months than you would have if you withdrew at random tines.\n\nThe paper does not have the same boundary conditions that I had to apply for trading as we do it, but the process of derivation is similar in some areas. And for those that this makes sense to, my solution was luckily a closed form one. It was beautiful, but a bit hefty.  \n\nIf you are up for a challenge, read some of this paper.",
      "author": {
        "id": "1376587708050309132",
        "name": "sentientali",
        "discriminator": "0000",
