    {
      "id": "1478979308138795008",
      "type": "Default",
      "timestamp": "2026-03-05T04:55:45.167+00:00",
      "timestampEdited": "2026-03-05T17:41:35.407+00:00",
      "callEndedTimestamp": null,
      "isPinned": false,
      "content": "JustLogic: A Comprehensive Benchmark for Evaluating Deductive Reasoning in Large Language Models (2025)\n\nThis paper alongside others show us that modern AI/LLMs such as GPT have weaker deductive reasoning when compared to the average human. \n\nDeductive reasoning paths, as stated in our materials is an important component for creating real, robust trading edges.\n\nIn plain terms:\nThis publication shows that models scores noticeably below the human average for the deductive branch of intelligence which confirmed my suspicions. This is why I don't like to do nuanced reasoning or research with AI and neither should any member. Our brains are superior, atleast for now.",
      "author": {
        "id": "231881969250598913",
        "name": "sentienttradingsociety",
        "discriminator": "0000",
        "nickname": "SentientRon",
        "color": "#0088FF",
        "isBot": false,
        "roles": [
